  "answer": "ANSWER: The canisters were the wrong shape. The command module's lithium hydroxide CO2 canisters were square, and the lunar module's were round, so they couldn't fit straight in. Engineers made an adapter (the \"mailbox\") from hoses, cardboard, plastic bags and tape. The crew built it by following instructions radioed up to them. (src: NASA Apollo 13 mission page, 2026-10-24)\nFILES: index.md, topics/co2-scrubber-adapter.md",
